WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.385
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:09.002
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.302 --> 00:00:15.553
Unit twenty-four: Causative Verb Patterns. Today you will choose between make, let, have, get and help.

4
00:00:15.853 --> 00:00:18.517
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.816
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:24.407
Make.

7
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:27.776
Make means to force someone to do something.

8
00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:29.814
The teacher made us stay.

9
00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:32.616
Your turn. Say: Make.

10
00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:36.468
Make.

11
00:00:37.217 --> 00:00:38.009
Let.

12
00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:40.575
Let means to allow.

13
00:00:41.183 --> 00:00:42.753
My parents let me go.

14
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.491
Your turn. Say: Let.

15
00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:49.091
Let.

16
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:50.665
Have.

17
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.242
Have means to arrange for someone to do something.

18
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.130
I had him fix it.

19
00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:58.835
Your turn. Say: Have.

20
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.364
Have.

21
00:01:03.117 --> 00:01:03.862
Get.

22
00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.395
Get means to persuade someone to do something.

23
00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:09.240
I got her to help.

24
00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:12.468
Your turn. Say: Get.

25
00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:16.009
Get.

26
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:17.554
Help.

27
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:21.118
Help means to assist, with or without to.

28
00:01:21.717 --> 00:01:23.171
She helped me (to) study.

29
00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.925
Your turn. Say: Help.

30
00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:29.559
Help.

31
00:01:30.317 --> 00:01:31.504
Bare infinitive.

32
00:01:32.517 --> 00:01:34.888
Bare infinitive means the verb without to.

33
00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:38.205
Make him go. Go is a bare infinitive.

34
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:42.119
Your turn. Say: Bare infinitive.

35
00:01:44.967 --> 00:01:46.235
Bare infinitive.

36
00:01:46.983 --> 00:01:47.892
Permission.

37
00:01:48.883 --> 00:01:50.813
Permission means allowing something.

38
00:01:51.417 --> 00:01:52.731
They gave permission.

39
00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:55.795
Your turn. Say: Permission.

40
00:01:58.633 --> 00:01:59.553
Permission.

41
00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:01.190
Force.

42
00:02:02.183 --> 00:02:04.462
Force means pressure that makes someone act.

43
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.202
She used force.

44
00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:09.272
Your turn. Say: Force.

45
00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:13.030
Force.

46
00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:17.693
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.594
Visal, what did your parents make or let you do as a child?

48
00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:33.117
My parents made me do homework before play, and they let me stay up late on weekends. Make means force, and let means allow. Both take a bare infinitive.

49
00:02:34.217 --> 00:02:35.717
What about have and get?

50
00:02:36.817 --> 00:02:48.260
Have someone do something is to arrange it: I had the mechanic check the car. Get someone to do something is to persuade: I got my brother to help. Get takes a to-infinitive.

51
00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.409
And help?

52
00:02:51.517 --> 00:03:05.039
Help takes either: She helped me study or helped me to study. But the passive of make requires to: He was made to apologise. Also note the causative with objects: have the car repaired.

53
00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.724
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:16.040
Grammar focus: Causatives: make and let and have plus object plus base verb; get plus object plus to-infinitive.

55
00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.526
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.217 --> 00:03:20.239
My parents made me do my homework.

57
00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.674
They let me stay up late.

58
00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:25.327
I got my brother to help me.

59
00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:34.799
Make, let and have take object + bare infinitive. Get takes object + to-infinitive. Help takes either. Passive make takes to.

60
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.284
Be careful! Don't say: She made me to leave.

61
00:03:40.233 --> 00:03:42.512
Say: She made me leave.

62
00:03:42.812 --> 00:03:44.474
Use the bare infinitive.

63
00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:47.942
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:48.733 --> 00:03:49.920
Rules at Home.

65
00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:52.556
My parents made me do my homework first.

66
00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:55.949
They let me watch television on weekends.

67
00:03:56.933 --> 00:03:59.548
Sometimes I got my brother to help with chores.

68
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:02.916
My mother had the neighbour repair the fence.

69
00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.457
These patterns show who controls the action.

70
00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:11.499
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.303
The teacher made us blank quietly.

72
00:04:14.603 --> 00:04:17.908
A, work. B, to work. C, working.

73
00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:23.118
The answer is A: work.

74
00:04:24.283 --> 00:04:25.818
She let me blank early.

75
00:04:26.118 --> 00:04:29.249
A, leave. B, to leave. C, leaving.

76
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.765
The answer is A: leave.

77
00:04:35.917 --> 00:04:37.254
I got him blank me.

78
00:04:37.554 --> 00:04:40.813
A, help. B, to help. C, helping.

79
00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:46.389
The answer is B: to help.

80
00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.770
Which means 'arrange for someone to do it'?

81
00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:53.224
A, have. B, make. C, let.

82
00:04:56.767 --> 00:04:58.755
The answer is A: have.

83
00:04:59.917 --> 00:05:02.926
According to the reading, what did the neighbour repair?

84
00:05:03.226 --> 00:05:06.822
A, the fence. B, the roof. C, the car.

85
00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:12.587
The answer is A: the fence.

86
00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:17.010
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.372
What did your parents make or let you do as a child?

88
00:05:29.183 --> 00:05:30.742
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:31.042 --> 00:05:42.476
My parents made me tidy my room every day. They let me play outside until dark. I also got my brother to help me with homework. These patterns show who had power.

90
00:05:42.776 --> 00:05:44.579
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:45.483 --> 00:05:54.695
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and causatives: make and let and have plus object plus base verb; get plus object plus to-infinitive.

92
00:05:54.995 --> 00:05:58.925
Today's value is gratitude. Say thank you for your home and family.

93
00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:02.295
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:05.247
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

